{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e","id":4986,"title":"Magic in 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-07T05:39:15-08:00","id":4986,"title":"Magic in 2e","content":"I don\u2019t want to see a Magic Purview in 2e. I\u2019d like what\u2019s currently the Magic Purview to be replaced by a Fortune Purview. That said, I don\u2019t want Magic to go away. Instead of a Magic Purview, I want a Birthright that provides an activity-based means of accessing Boons, much like Relics provide item-based access. Unlike other Birthrights, these Rituals wouldn\u2019t be tangible and so could never be taken away from the scion. But Boons activated through a Ritual would have to meet special criteria every time they\u2019re activated. These criteria would, of course, depend at least in part on the Pantheon from which the Ritual originated: a Ritual of the Tuatha de Danaan would feel quite different from a Ritual of the Aesir or the Pesedjet. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d also like to see the mechanics for Rituals to be designed to allow for mortal priests to have at least limited access to them. This would imply that a practitioner of a given Ritual should be able to access Boons that his Legend otherwise wouldn\u2019t permit, possibly by layering on additional requirements for each level by which the desired Boon exceeds the character\u2019s Legend. Or it would imply that there are mortals (suitable for use as Guides) who have a limited variant of Legend that\u2019s good only for providing access to Boons: no Epic Attributes or Knacks, and none of the other benefits that Legend usually provides. <br /> <br /> A \u201cGod of Magic\u201d wouldn\u2019t be defined as such by a Purview, but rather by a Knack that makes him a virtuoso when it comes to inventing new Rituals. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T06:50:39-08:00","id":5032,"title":"","content":"One of the writers has said that magic (small &quot;m&quot;) is part of the mechanics for Scion: Origin, and will cross over all three tiers above. There's also mention of mortal sorcerers and holy people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T09:29:38-08:00","id":8141,"title":"","content":"I definitely agree that it needs further development in the new edition. It was one of the aspects I felt was most lacking and really just sort of tacked on as an afterthought despite the importance of magic and ritual for a game that is dealing with religion. I like the idea of having some sort of general power listed as a description and then having specific criteria for how a Scion would go about conducting the ritual based on their Pantheon to keep it from just being some vague manipulation of Fate, as it seems to be now.<br /> <br /> I don't know about replacing access to Magic with or denoting specialization with Knacks over Boons though. Even among supernatural beings in mythology, magic tends to have its own special corner that I think a Boon represents more.<br /> <br /> Though, I do agree that the development of mortal priests/followers needs to happen as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1007-merinoc","name":"Merinoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T10:00:36-08:00","id":8166,"title":"","content":"marin: where do the devs post most of their spoilers?<br /> <br /> Merinoc: the problem with a Magic Purview is that it becomes a \u201cdo anything\u201d Purview, or it\u2019s too narrowly defined to be what\u2019s implied when you say \u201cmagic\u201d. I suppose that one could retool it to be more of a \u201cmeta-magic\u201d Purview, though: that is, the Purview of Magic doesn\u2019t grant access to spells or rituals; those would be available through Birthrights as I described above. Rather, the Magic Purview would be about <i>enhancing</i> your spells and rituals: the ability to be a virtuoso as described above, or the ability to cast spells with fewer trappings than others would need. In short, the Magic Purview wouldn\u2019t be a spell list; it would be a means to upgrade your spells.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T10:17:00-08:00","id":8187,"title":"","content":"Over on the Origins post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T10:31:52-08:00","id":8202,"title":"","content":"Ah. Think the link misfired, PH (had it happen to me; click the &quot;A&quot; on the commentbox, and use the link icon there).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/258-scion-origin-whats-the-deal\">Here's the thread in question.</a><br /> <br /> And this's the relevant quote from Neall:<br /> <br /> <i>We're still largely deciding what goes into Origin and what goes into Hero, but the idea is that the bare bones of the mechanical system will be laid out in Origin. <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The book can be used to create and play urban fantasy stories, and will include the setting(s) for doing just that. If creatures are handled in the book, they'll be beings of myth but low Legend - dryads, satyrs, and the like. And, yes, pre-Visitation Scions, but also holy men and women of the pantheons, sorcerers who seek to steal the power of the gods, and those bound by Fate (your Oedipuses, your Cassandras, your Arjunas). Some of its mechanics will include not just the baseline rules, but also rules for things that cross over and access all three tiers of play - magic and Fate among them.</span></span></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":51,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","user":"marin","date":". 11-11-2013, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T10:41:15-08:00","id":8213,"title":"","content":"The whole idea of a &quot;Magic&quot; Purview is kinda laughable when the other Purviews are throwing fireballs, teleporting, creating illusions, summoning beasts, etc. They're all magical. Every single Scion is a &quot;magician&quot; as long as they've invested in <i>any</i> Purview. Purviews are the 'Magic' of Scion, not any one specific Purview.<br /> <br /> At various times, people have come on the forums and asked &quot;how do I make a magician? I don't see how it works!&quot; because they're looking at the Magic Purview (duh) and not seeing fireballs, teleporting, illusions, necromancy, etc. That's all under other Purviews. In other games, &quot;magic&quot; is a specific thing that <i>some</i> classes do. In Scion, it's not. Everyone has magic, everyone does magic and you have to decide what <i>kind</i> of magic you want. <br /> <br /> You could replace the idea of a Magic Purview with something like Rituals, but that introduces a whole new category of powers, unless you decide it's just another way to use Boons and get some kinda bonus. If you use a Ritual instead of a Boon, you can access (Legend) Rank stuff instead of (Legend -1) Rank stuff. I don't know that such an idea really offers that much. I think the difference between a Norse PC and an Egyptian PC is already pretty evident in how they play, their Relics, their PSP, their Followers/Guides/Creatures/Allies, etc and what kind of concepts that Pantheon embraces. There could certainly be more Pantheon-specific Boons in APP's, like Riastriad and Fury of War, but I don't think there needs to be a system for ritualized magic when a lot of cultures don't have such a system in place for their Gods to follow. Their <i>human followers</i> might have had rituals to perform, but that's what mortal magicians are for, not Scions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T11:57:20-08:00","id":8280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8213#post8213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole idea of a &quot;Magic&quot; Purview is kinda laughable when the other Purviews are throwing fireballs, teleporting, creating illusions, summoning beasts, etc. They're all magical. Every single Scion is a &quot;magician&quot; as long as they've invested in <i>any</i> Purview. Purviews are the 'Magic' of Scion, not any one specific Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much, yeah. I don\u2019t <i>quite</i> agree with this, because performing a ritual to summon lightning down from the sky feels different from firing lightning bolts out of your trusty revolver or shooting lightning from your arse; but yeah, the ability to call lightning is something that comes from the Sky Purview. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8213#post8213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could replace the idea of a Magic Purview with something like Rituals, but that introduces a whole new category of powers, unless you decide it's just another way to use Boons and get some kinda bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026which is exactly what I was suggesting. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8213#post8213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you use a Ritual instead of a Boon, you can access (Legend) Rank stuff instead of (Legend -1) Rank stuff. I don't know that such an idea really offers that much.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that\u2019s the way it\u2019s implemented, then it doesn\u2019t really offer much. But what if the cap were, say, (Legend + 3), or if the cap was removed altogether and replaced by increasingly stringent conditions that must be met before the Boon can be accessed? That could make it worthwhile, at least until your Legend tops out. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8213#post8213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the difference between a Norse PC and an Egyptian PC is already pretty evident in how they play, their Relics, their PSP, their Followers/Guides/Creatures/Allies, etc and what kind of concepts that Pantheon embraces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed; and I\u2019m very grateful that the game does this. I also think that explaining how Norse magic and Egyptian magic differ would further enrich the game. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8213#post8213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There could certainly be more Pantheon-specific Boons in APP's, like Riastriad and Fury of War, but I don't think there needs to be a system for ritualized magic when a lot of cultures don't have such a system in place for their Gods to follow. Their <i>human followers</i> might have had rituals to perform, but that's what mortal magicians are for, not Scions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and no. Certainly, magic rituals aren\u2019t the <i>primary</i> way for gods to access their Boons. But there <i>are</i> instances in mythology of gods using magic; and the lower you get on the Legend scale, the more frequent magicians are: you don\u2019t have to go all the way down to Legend 0 to find them. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T13:27:39-08:00","id":8331,"title":"","content":"I think the last point there is a huge part of the problem though. If the most prolific use of ritualistic magic instead of divine power magic is at lower Legend, then it seems silly to have a Magic Purview that will scale with increasing Legend.<br /> <br /> To me it seems like a solution might be something more like Thaumaturgy in Exalted. Something you don't need to be a Scion to use (so it gets to be a major toy at Origins level play), and lower Legend Scions might use it as a sort of grab-bag for occult oriented Scions to not have to buy lots of little powers, but upper level Legend characters generally don't bother because they can do better with other options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T13:52:10-08:00","id":8350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8331#post8331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the last point there is a huge part of the problem though. If the most prolific use of ritualistic magic instead of divine power magic is at lower Legend, then it seems silly to have a Magic Purview that will scale with increasing Legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going back to the first sentence of this topic: \u201cI don\u2019t want to see a Magic Purview in 2e.\u201d If we <i>do</i> end up with one, it ought to be more about affecting how magic works than about casting spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8331#post8331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me it seems like a solution might be something more like Thaumaturgy in Exalted. Something you don't need to be a Scion to use (so it gets to be a major toy at Origins level play), and lower Legend Scions might use it as a sort of grab-bag for occult oriented Scions to not have to buy lots of little powers, but upper level Legend characters generally don't bother because they can do better with other options.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. But again, there are examples in mythology of gods using magic; so it shouldn\u2019t be completely useless even as high as Legend 9. (As an example, Norse \u201crunemasters\u201d are said to emulate the example set by Odin when they practice their magic.)<br /> <br /> Really though, the main thing I want from magic in <b>Scion 2e</b> is for, e.g., the magic of the Loa to feel like voodoo. I\u2019ve had my fill of \u201cgeneric magic\u201d in <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>, and I\u2019ll go to <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> if I want \u201cmagic is whatever you believe it to be\u201d. For <b>Scion</b>, I want each Pantheon\u2019s magic to be a reasonably faithful presentation of the belief systems of the people who gave rise to that Pantheon\u2019s mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-11-2013, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T19:59:23-08:00","id":8567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8350#post8350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want each Pantheon\u2019s magic to be a reasonably faithful presentation of the belief systems of the people who gave rise to that Pantheon\u2019s mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really feasible to build into a system designed to cover every single Pantheon ever, all at once. The system itself <b>has</b> to be Pantheon-neutral. It's up to the players and the Storyteller to narrate the effects of their Boons in thematic and appropriate ways. You \u200bdon't have to just call lightning down with Sky, you can write &quot;And my Enemy was Smote by Lightning&quot; on a papyrus scroll in ancient hieroglyphics, thus binding your words into the very fabric of reality through the magic of the written word... and that's just how you, as an Egyptian Scion, happen to use Levin Fury.<br /> <br /> Odin throwing runes is just stunting his Prophecy/Mystery roll, or maybe using a Relic to add bonuses. Aaand... um. That's all I got for Gods performing ritual magic. Even Isis doesn't perform ritual magic that I can recall off-hand. She performs &quot;magic&quot;, certainly, but it's just general supernatural stuff that humans can't do. Purviews, basically. When Circe turns Odysseus's men into pigs, she doesn't use a ritual, she just zaps 'em with her magic wand. I really can't think of many times that Gods perform ritualized sorcery and when they use props, it's generally Relics that are adding extra dice or something to their Purviews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T20:34:13-08:00","id":8577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8567#post8567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not really feasible to build into a system designed to cover every single Pantheon ever, all at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if <b>Scion</b> was designed to cover every single Pantheon ever, all at once, you might have a point. But it isn\u2019t: it\u2019s designed primarily to handle European-style Pantheons, and it requires you to squeeze other Pantheons into that mold. Yet, despite this, it still manages to make each Pantheon feel distinct. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8567#post8567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The system itself <b>has</b> to be Pantheon-neutral. It's up to the players and the Storyteller to narrate the effects of their Boons in thematic and appropriate ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>To a limited extent, yes. But you don\u2019t have to take it to the extreme of the magic system being <i>totally</i> Pantheon-neutral; nor do you need to rely <i>solely</i> on the Storyteller and players to supply the cultural distinctions. There are more choices here than \u201csingle homogenized system for everything\u201d and \u201ceach Pantheon has a separate and unique system of its own\u201d. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T20:46:53-08:00","id":8579,"title":"","content":"It actually doesn't handle &quot;European-style&quot; Pantheons very well either because they don't even fall into the neat &quot;Heaven = Up, Hell = Down&quot; system that is so thoroughly ingrained into popular Western culture. The Greeks didn't have that, the Norse didn't, the Gauls and Irish don't... no one really does <i>except</i> Abrahamic religions, but that's the lens most of the writers and players are coming from. So, that's what happens. <br /> <br /> And, yes, there are options besides a totally different magic system for each Pantheon and one homogenious system. Scion does that already. It has Pantheon-Specific Purviews, Birthrights, fluff and flavor on a per-character basis and the option to create your own Boons, Knacks and other powers that customize your characters and NPCs. It even has Pantheon-unique Boons for existing Purviews.<br /> <br /> I really don't see how adding a system for ritualized performances of Boons that allow access to higher level Boons or increase the power of ritualized Boons adds more cultural diversity. It would have to be just as bland and generic as the rest of the system, and then be <i>customized</i> by players and Storytellers to fit each culture. You'd still have to add in the poppets, runestones, i-ching and ifa divination bowls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T20:48:07-08:00","id":8580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8350#post8350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really though, the main thing I want from magic in <b>Scion 2e</b> is for, e.g., the magic of the Loa to feel like voodoo.<br /> ...<br /> For <b>Scion</b>, I want each Pantheon\u2019s magic to be a reasonably faithful presentation of the belief systems of the people who gave rise to that Pantheon\u2019s mythology.</div> </div> </div> </div>You and me both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T21:48:04-08:00","id":8604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8579#post8579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It actually doesn't handle &quot;European-style&quot; Pantheons very well either because they don't even fall into the neat &quot;Heaven = Up, Hell = Down&quot; system that is so thoroughly ingrained into popular Western culture. The Greeks didn't have that, the Norse didn't, the Gauls and Irish don't... no one really does <i>except</i> Abrahamic religions, but that's the lens most of the writers and players are coming from. So, that's what happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>If by \u201cHeaven\u201d you mean \u201cthe realm of the gods\u201d, and by \u201cHell\u201d you mean \u201cthe land of the dead\u201d, then the Greeks certainly had something like that (Mount Olypus on the one hand; Orpheus descending into the underworld on the other hand), as do the Norse (I don\u2019t know where they pictured Hel\u2019s domain to be; but Asgard was somewhere over the rainbow). I wouldn\u2019t know about the Gauls; from what I gather, no one does. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8579#post8579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, yes, there are options besides a totally different magic system for each Pantheon and one homogenious system. Scion does that already. It has Pantheon-Specific Purviews, Birthrights, fluff and flavor on a per-character basis and the option to create your own Boons, Knacks and other powers that customize your characters and NPCs. It even has Pantheon-unique Boons for existing Purviews.</div> </div> </div> </div>You\u2019ve mentioned this several times already; I haven\u2019t responded to it because I don\u2019t disagree. I just don\u2019t see it as an argument for not diversifying the representation of magic in the game. It\u2019s as if you\u2019re saying \u201cwe have enough diversification in the game already; more diversity would be a bad thing\u201d. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8579#post8579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't see how adding a system for ritualized performances of Boons that allow access to higher level Boons or increase the power of ritualized Boons adds more cultural diversity. It would have to be just as bland and generic as the rest of the system, and then be <i>customized</i> by players and Storytellers to fit each culture. You'd still have to add in the poppets, runestones, i-ching and ifa divination bowls.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends entirely on the implementation. For one example of a magic system that allows for different cultural flavors to be baked in, look at <b>Dark Ages: Mage</b>. Each Fellowship in that game has a Foundation and a set of Pillars; even before you get to the magical tools, the choice of Foundation and Pillars gives a sense of how that Fellowship\u2019s magic differs from the other Fellowships. The Valdaermen Foundation is Sacrifice, and their Pillars are Runes; the Messianic Voices\u2019 Foundation is Divinity, and their Pillars are Archangels; the Old Faith\u2019s Foundation is Spontaneity, and its Pillars are the Seasons; and so on. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T22:47:09-08:00","id":8626,"title":"","content":"So what are you calling magic? PSPs? Boons? Something else? Right now, each Pantheon's magic does represent their culture via their PSP, their signature-styled Boons and the Birthrights they bestow. If you're talking about something as complex as a whole second system of powers designed to reflect each culture's views of what &quot;magic&quot; is, I think that's going too far and making the game too complex.<br /> <br /> Too much diversity can be bad because it makes the game system cluttered and confusing. Scion already has a lot of issues, and I'd rather see a very strong, well-designed Purview system that works for <b>all</b> Pantheons and then can be customized on a per-character and per-Pantheon basis with unique, signature Boons and Birthrights. Don't forget that we <i>also</i> have Knacks and Epics in Scion that represent things almost as &quot;magical&quot; as Purviews, especially the Social Knacks and Mental Knacks since they often stand in for the lack of an Emotion/Love Purview and a Crafting Purview. <br /> <br /> Does Scion really need <i>three</i> different systems of powers? Rituals, Boons and Knacks all together? That seems like overkill to me, and just another thing to spend XP on. I agree, it'd be nice if Loa felt like Loa and Egyptians like Egyptians, but I think the ability to do that <i>already exists</i>, it just isn't being used as well as it could be. There aren't <i>enough</i> Boons, especially unique signature Boons like Fury of War and Riastriad. In fact, those are just about the <i>only</i> signature Boons because no one but the Norse got their own book. With more Boons added in each Purview, they can feel more &quot;magical&quot; and take over a lot of the things the Magic Purview used to do. With more Relics and other Birthrights, they can add more flavor.<br /> <br /> I want to see diversity and uniqueness, but I don't think a whole new system is the way to add that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T00:03:28-08:00","id":8643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8626#post8626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what are you calling magic? PSPs? Boons? Something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> What I\u2019m calling \u201cmagic\u201d is a specific flavor of supernatural power, defined less in terms of what it can do (which is what Boons are all about) than how it is done (e.g., symbolic trappings, rituals, sacrifices, auspicious times and places, etc. \u2014 as opposed to wielding an item). That\u2019s why I was thinking in terms of handling it as a kind of Birthright.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8626#post8626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now, each Pantheon's magic does represent their culture via their PSP, their signature-styled Boons and the Birthrights they bestow. If you're talking about something as complex as a whole second system of powers designed to reflect each culture's views of what &quot;magic&quot; is, I think that's going too far and making the game too complex.</div> </div> </div> </div>We\u2019ll see. I have some thoughts about how such a system might work <i>without</i> overcomplicating things; but that\u2019s a subjective judgment call. And ultimately, what matters isn\u2019t what <i>my</i> ideas are, but what the <i>developers</i> are thinking. Which is where Neall\u2019s recent post comes in: while it\u2019s not a promise that they <i>will</i>\u200b include what I\u2019m hoping for, it indicates that they\u2019re at least investigating the possibility. Which implies that they don\u2019t consider it to be an obviously flawed idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8626#post8626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too much diversity can be bad because it makes the game system cluttered and confusing. Scion already has a lot of issues, and I'd rather see a very strong, well-designed Purview system that works for <b>all</b> Pantheons and then can be customized on a per-character and per-Pantheon basis with unique, signature Boons and Birthrights. Don't forget that we <i>also</i> have Knacks and Epics in Scion that represent things almost as &quot;magical&quot; as Purviews, especially the Social Knacks and Mental Knacks since they often stand in for the lack of an Emotion/Love Purview and a Crafting Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think at this point you should define what <i>you</i> mean by \u201cmagic\u201d; because you seem to be treating the term as being entirely interchangeable with \u201csupernatural\u201d.<br /> <br /> \u200bI, too, would like a robust, well-designed Purview system that works for all Pantheons which can then be customized with signature Boons and Birthrights. But I wouldn\u2019t want to stop there. It would do a great job expanding what magic (and other supernatural powers) can do; but it would do nothing to address how magic is practiced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8626#post8626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to see diversity and uniqueness, but I don't think a whole new system is the way to add that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t know if it is or not. I <i>do</i> agree that dedicating as much word-count to a fully self-contained magic system that duplicates a lot of Boons would probably be a mistake \u2014 which is why I\u2019m against a Magic Purview that\u2019s essentially a spell list, and would prefer to avoid a Magic Purview at all. But I could be wrong about that: it may well be that a third system, existing alongside Knacks and Boons, is the way to go. Or not. Personally, I\u2019d prefer something that leverages the existing Boons to represent magic, which is where my Ritual brainstorming came in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T00:28:41-08:00","id":8653,"title":"","content":"But the existing Boons don't represent magic they <i>are</i> magic as Scion goes. They <i>are</i> how the Norse cast runes, the Loa ride their worshippers and the Egyptians harness the power of True Names. A third system just to represent something that can be perfectly well represented with the existing systems is just an extra, unnecessary, layer of complexity in an already complex game. I define magic as &quot;supernatural powers that humans cannot express&quot;. Humans can be strong and sexy and charismatic and smart, but they can't summon up sunlight or throw lightning or banish someone into shadows. <br /> <br /> I think ritual magic, sacrifices, etc, can all be dealt with as personal customization, unique Boons, Birthrights and other such trappings. They don't need a devoted system because any such system would have to be immensely complex to cover all the varieties of such rituals across dozens of cultures <i>or</i> it would have to be just as bland and boring as the system you want to diversify. The kinda stuff you're suggesting, like increased access to stronger boons or whatever else, that's not culturally specific in its <i>effect</i>, it would only be culturally specific in its <i>fluff</i>, which can be done already with the existing system.<br /> <br /> Should it be possible to get a bonus for special trappings? Yes, Relics. Rituals, sacrifices, performing actions at certain times and places? Yes. Stunts. I don't see a need for a more complicated system to implement such things because such a system wouldn't be any more culturally diverse than the existing Purviews and Birthrights have the <i>potential</i> to be. I hope that the developers expand Purviews and Birthrights and use <i>them</i> to make the &quot;magic&quot; of the Loa feel like voodoo and the &quot;magic&quot; of the Pesedjet feel Egyptian. It would actually be far more <i>limiting</i> to have all that diversity tied up in some Ritual-Magic system, especially for cultures that <i>don't practice ritual magic</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T01:54:24-08:00","id":8679,"title":"","content":"Perhaps if the notion of Relics and Stunts were generalized a bit from their intuitive definitions (e.g., \u201cRelics\u201d that represent a type of thing that can be fairly easily acquired and lost, rather than unique items that you don\u2019t dare lose, and \u201cStunts\u201d that have nothing to do with attempting something spectacular), then yes, they could be used as ways of at least partially implementing a magic system. Even aside from the counterintuitive use of terms, I don\u2019t think it would be quite enough (e.g., it doesn\u2019t give a means for <b>Origins</b>' minimal-Legend sorcerers and holy men to practice magic); but it\u2019s an interesting idea. <br /> <br /> Speaking of unintuitive names, I should probably speak of Practices rather than Rituals when discussing the \u201cmagic as Birthright\u201d idea. Rituals are just one of several possible conditions that a sorcerer might need to meet in order to access a Boon through a Practice; and the selection of what sorts of conditions would need to be met would be a key part of defining the feel of the magic. I could probably write up the whole system I\u2019m thinking of in one or two pages, possibly less. <br /> <br /> And those aren\u2019t the only options. I\u2019m sure the developers have their own ideas on the subject, and they are likely to have nothing in common with either of the proposals we\u2019ve made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T09:48:11-08:00","id":8886,"title":"","content":"I... have never considered Relics as something &quot;easily acquired and lost&quot; or Stunts as &quot;having nothing to do with attempting something spectacular&quot;. The exact opposite, in fact. <b>Any</b> Birthright is something that is <b>not</b> easy to acquire and is devastating if lost. Thor would be one sad beard without Mjolnir and what would poor Tezcatlipoca do without his mirror? How would Freyr get around without Gullinbursti? And Stunts... well, their systematic definition <i>is</i> attempting something spectacular. I cannot understand where you're coming from, dude. How can Relics and Stunts <b>not</b> be awesome, amazing and of epic importance?<br /> <br /> To sum up my argument: I think if you have a system that defines <i>how</i> characters can do something instead of <i>what</i> they can do, that's limiting the players. I would rather not see such a thing and leave it up to individual STs and players to determine <i>how</i> a Boon functions and consider any ritualized practices to be stunts and other situational bonuses, not an entirely new system of powers. Maybe the Loa doesn't <i>want</i> to use voodoo and he wants to practice techno-sympathetic magic via microchips and HTML. Leave that up to him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":235,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","user":"Telgar","date":". 11-12-2013, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T12:03:16-08:00","id":9047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8886#post8886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... have never considered Relics as something &quot;easily acquired and lost&quot; or Stunts as &quot;having nothing to do with attempting something spectacular&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise; which is why I thought it was strange that you were suggesting the use of Relics to represent something that\u2019s potentially easy to acquire or lose (i.e., the physical trappings of a spell) and the use of Stunts to represent activities that probably aren\u2019t spectacular (i.e., rituals, sacrifices, etc.) \u2014 flavorful, yes; but not the sort of thing I think of when I hear \u201cStunt\u201d. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8886#post8886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To sum up my argument: I think if you have a system that defines <i>how</i> characters can do something instead of <i>what</i> they can do, that's limiting the players.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you <i>already</i> have such a system in <b>Scion</b>: if you don\u2019t have an appropriate Relic to channel a Boon through, you can\u2019t use that Boon. This defines how you use your Boons: you channel them through your Relics. The suggestion I\u2019m considering here is to treat the practice of magic as an alternative to channeling your Boons through your Relics. That doesn\u2019t limit options; it <i>adds</i> options. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=8886#post8886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would rather not see such a thing and leave it up to individual STs and players to determine <i>how</i> a Boon functions and consider any ritualized practices to be stunts and other situational bonuses, not an entirely new system of powers. Maybe the Loa doesn't <i>want</i> to use voodoo and he wants to practice techno-sympathetic magic via microchips and HTML. Leave that up to him.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u201cMagic works exactly how you imagine it works\u201d is a <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> thing, as I see it. Given that <b>Scion</b> is all about fidelity to myths and legends, magic in <b>Scion</b> should work the way the myths and legends say it works<sup><span style=\"font-size:9px\">1</span></sup>. Techno-sympathetic magic has about as much of a place in <b>Scion</b> as a Pantheon featuring Santa Claus or Uncle Sam. <br /> <br /> Now, should a Loa be locked into <i>just</i> voodoo as her means of practicing magic? That depends on your views on mixing cultural elements in a single character. I could maybe see a Loa who has studied magic at the feet of a mentor who is aligned with the Aesir and thus adhering to the trappings and practices of Norse sorcery; but it shouldn\u2019t be that she uses runecrafting instead of voodoo on a whim. Likewise, there\u2019s the question of how compatible different styles of magic are: can a sorcerer practice <i>both</i> voodoo <i>and</i> runecrafting? I\u2019d be inclined to say no; but I can see decent arguments for allowing it, concept permitting. Either way, it would be an implementation detail, to be decided by the developers and overruled by the Storyteller if he disagrees \u2014 just like the Storyteller is free to introduce a techno-sympathetic magic style or the likes of Santa Claus into his game if he so chooses. <br /> <br /> Also, I\u2019m not advocating an entirely new system of powers<sup><span style=\"font-size:10px\">2</span></sup>; what I\u2019m picturing would use the same Boons that everything else does to define what you can do when you practice magic. The only \u201cnew system\u201d that would be added would be summed up in a Birthright write-up (or something similar) that would be no more extensive than Relics, and possibly less so. <br /> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:9px\"><sup><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"font-size:9px\">1</span> </span></sup><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Ideally, of course. In practice, complete fidelity is unworkable; but that doesn\u2019t mean you can\u2019t get reasonably close, or that you shouldn\u2019t even try. <br /> <sup>2</sup> I\u2019m also not opposed to it, if the developers can come up with one that\u2019s suitably concise. </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T13:14:00-08:00","id":9087,"title":"","content":"What I did for my Scion game was convert Dark Ages: Mage over to the Scion system. It gives you culturally specific magic that isn't overwhelmingly powerful, which is exactly what I wanted.<br /> <br /> Also, the <i>reason</i> that I wanted a magic system for Scion is because I want antagonists that have a powerset that isn't exactly the same as that of the player characters. I made a martial arts system for the same reason. I get really bored with the idea that every single thing in the universe uses some combination of knacks, boons, and special, one-off powers to define their abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/794-el-pinko-grande","name":"el pinko grande","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar794_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T13:35:04-08:00","id":9114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9047#post9047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The suggestion I\u2019m considering here is to treat the practice of magic as an alternative to channeling your Boons through your Relics. That doesn\u2019t limit options; it <i>adds</i> options.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this has merits, but I don't think it really solves the general problem. Magical rituals that replace the need for a Relic to access a Boon is a good idea, but it doesn't accomplish what you seem to want. There's no reason for the gods to use it to resonate with the myth of magic using deities. It's also pretty inconvenient compared to Relics, meaning most PCs will never opt for this path. Why would I want to spend an hour each time I want to strike an enemy with lightning instead of just getting a Relic and being able to do that whenever I want instantly?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cMagic works exactly how you imagine it works\u201d is a <b>Mage: the Ascension</b> thing, as I see it. </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's fair. Scion is just like Mage in that it is trying to get lots of disparate myths to cooperate in a single game. This inevitably leads to a lot of &quot;same mechanics, different fluff&quot; rules, because that's the only reasonable way to accomplish the base line options of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given that <b>Scion</b> is all about fidelity to myths and legends, magic in <b>Scion</b> should work the way the myths and legends say it works<sup><span style=\"font-size:9px\">1</span></sup>. Techno-sympathetic magic has about as much of a place in <b>Scion</b> as a Pantheon featuring Santa Claus or Uncle Sam. </div> </div> </div>Erm... not a fan of the Scion Companion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T15:58:32-08:00","id":9257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9114#post9114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this has merits, but I don't think it really solves the general problem. Magical rituals that replace the need for a Relic to access a Boon is a good idea, but it doesn't accomplish what you seem to want. There's no reason for the gods to use it to resonate with the myth of magic using deities. It's also pretty inconvenient compared to Relics, meaning most PCs will never opt for this path. Why would I want to spend an hour each time I want to strike an enemy with lightning instead of just getting a Relic and being able to do that whenever I want instantly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Practices would be usable without needing a one-of-a-kind item, and they\u2019d be able to access Boons that otherwise require more Legend than the character has. This would be needed to let mortal sorcerers actually do something with sorcery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9114#post9114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think that's fair. Scion is just like Mage in that it is trying to get lots of disparate myths to cooperate in a single game. This inevitably leads to a lot of &quot;same mechanics, different fluff&quot; rules, because that's the only reasonable way to accomplish the base line options of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t have a problem with \u201csame mechanics, different fluff\u201d as long as the mechanics are sufficiently flexible to allow for different fluff to have different effects. My main issue was the idea that a scion\u2019s magical practices should be left entirely up to the player, and that the differences between various practices should be treated <i>entirely</i> as a matter of window dressing. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9114#post9114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erm... not a fan of the Scion Companion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a fan of the National Pantheons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T16:22:39-08:00","id":9273,"title":"","content":"\u200bA ritual sacrifice to power your magic isn't an awesome thing? Timing your use of Darkness Boons to a solar eclipse isn't legendary? The runestones carved from a jotun's icy bones aren't a powerful item? Relics and Stunts are perfectly suited to what you're talking about. If all it takes to satisfy ritual requirements to cast your version of magic is a bed sheet and some rice paper, that's just a fluffy description and gets maybe a 1 die Stunt. Those don't have to be too badass. If you want to go all out, you get more dice.<br /> <br /> I won't argue the fidelity of any game system to world mythology, or the place of modern science in Scion, because that's another issue entirely. Two of them, in fact. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9257#post9257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t have a problem with \u201csame mechanics, different fluff\u201d as long as the mechanics are sufficiently flexible to allow for different fluff to have different effects. My main issue was the idea that a scion\u2019s magical practices should be left entirely up to the player, and that the differences between various practices should be treated <i>entirely</i> as a matter of window dressing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say you don't have a problem with the idea, then list all your problems with that idea. The mechanics of Birthrights and Boons are incredibly flexible, since each Boon does one specific thing. It doesn't do the specific thing you want? Write one that does. The entirely open-ended system of Boons (you can write an infinite number) is as flexible as anything gets, really. I'm not sure how you get <i>more flexible </i>than a system that functions on self-contained powers. Remember that in Scion, you don't buy &quot;up&quot; your Purviews. You don't have to go in order, and buy Fire 1, then Fire 2, then Fire 3. You just buy individual, self-packaged powers that have &quot;FIRE&quot; stamped on them. Just like Gifts in Werewolf, there's no need for a connection between any given Rank 1 Fire Boon and any given Rank 8 Fire Boon, so long as they're both Fire-ish. I don't know how that can be more flexible. You want to do X, then just figure out which of the Purviews covers X, match it to a Rank based on if it's Heroic, Demigodly or Divine, and write it up. <br /> <br /> So it's perfectly possible to write Egyptian Boons that don't make sense for non-Egyptians, just as Scion already gave us with the Irish and Norse War Boons. <br /> <br /> Aside from letting mortals use Boons beyond their Legend, what would your proposed system of ritualized magic offer that Boons and Birthrights can't provide if used properly, with imagination and creativity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T01:14:03-08:00","id":9527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9257#post9257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Practices would be usable without needing a one-of-a-kind item, and they\u2019d be able to access Boons that otherwise require more Legend than the character has. This would be needed to let mortal sorcerers actually do something with sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>An individual Relic might be a one-of-a-kind, but Relics themselves are clearly meant to be numerous enough that a Scion can access their Boons fairly easily.<br /> <br /> Also, how can you use Boons that you might not have the Legend for if they just replace Relics? If you can use Practices to access a Boon you couldn't have, it means Practices let you ignore having to buy Boons. That's going beyond an alternative to Relics and very much gets into creating a new power system in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My main issue was the idea that a scion\u2019s magical practices should be left entirely up to the player, and that the differences between various practices should be treated <i>entirely</i> as a matter of window dressing. </div> </div> </div>As a matter of rules, not in-game requirements, why shouldn't they just be window dressing? Why should a Norse Practice to bless the earth to grow abundant crops have a different mechanic/resolution than a Greek one? They absolutely should look different, and have different ritual requirements, but why should they have different rules?<br /> <br /> Where is the value in them being different in game terms?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not a fan of the National Pantheons. </div> </div> </div>OK, but it still detracts from your point. Yes, the National Pantheons are a diversion from the core Scion themes, but the whole point is that Scion doesn't have to be limited to a strict ancient mythological foundation. Modern myths are still myths after all.<br /> <br /> Even the core game embraces a mix of modern and ancient. You have relic pistols and supernatural motorcycles together with ancient holy swords and sacred ancestral shields. If I can channel my Psychopomp Boons through a relic skateboard that lets me ride between worlds, what's wrong with a more technology themed magic Practice in the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T02:46:48-08:00","id":9550,"title":"","content":"This is going to be kind of a mixed response. On the one hand, I would certainly be interested in a ritual or practice system that allowed mundane or supernatural creatures to create phenomenon that is not inherent to themselves. On the other hand, after countless thousands of hours of playing, running, and working with Scion I have almost never seen a situation that could not be covered by a custom knack, a custom boon, a birthright, or good stunting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T09:10:52-08:00","id":9747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9527#post9527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, how can you use Boons that you might not have the Legend for if they just replace Relics? If you can use Practices to access a Boon you couldn't have, it means Practices let you ignore having to buy Boons. That's going beyond an alternative to Relics and very much gets into creating a new power system in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on what you mean by \u201ccreating a new power system.\u201d Arguably, <i>anything</i> that lets mortal sorcerers wield supernatural powers could be described as \u201ccreating a new power system\u201d. So either you\u2019re arguing against providing a way for mortal sorcerers to practice magic, or you mean something different by that phrase. Either way, it\u2019s a given right now that the developers intend to address magic in <b>Scion: Origins</b>, and that they intend to do so in a way that applies to all of the tiers of play, not just to mortals. I\u2019m trying to come up with some ideas for how such a thing might work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9527#post9527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a matter of rules, not in-game requirements, why shouldn't they just be window dressing? Why should a Norse Practice to bless the earth to grow abundant crops have a different mechanic/resolution than a Greek one? They absolutely should look different, and have different ritual requirements, but why should they have different rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, \u201chave different ritual requirements\u201d <i>is</i> \u201cdifferent rules\u201d. I\u2019m not asking for each Pantheon to have a hand-crafted, fully self-contained game engine for dealing with its magical practices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9527#post9527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, but it still detracts from your point. Yes, the National Pantheons are a diversion from the core Scion themes, but the whole point is that Scion doesn't have to be limited to a strict ancient mythological foundation. Modern myths are still myths after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>It only detracts from my point if National Pantheons are still a thing in <b>Scion 2e</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9527#post9527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the core game embraces a mix of modern and ancient. You have relic pistols and supernatural motorcycles together with ancient holy swords and sacred ancestral shields. If I can channel my Psychopomp Boons through a relic skateboard that lets me ride between worlds, what's wrong with a more technology themed magic Practice in the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have less of a problem with incorporating modern elements into traditional magical practices than I have with introducing whole new magical practices that are built around modern elements. If an individual Storyteller wants to do such a thing, more power to him! I might even make use of such homrbrewed systems myself. But if they\u2019re going to appear in an officially published <b>Scion</b> book, I would want it to be in a Shards-like supplement devoted specifically to using <b>Scion</b> for modern myths (as opposed to ancient myths in the modern world).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T09:33:27-08:00","id":9763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9747#post9747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So either you\u2019re arguing against providing a way for mortal sorcerers to practice magic, or you mean something different by that phrase.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a way for mortal sorcerers to practice magic is a separate issue from using Practice to access Boons instead of Relics.<br /> <br /> I'm not arguing against mortal sorcerers; however I don't think your idea works as a combination of mortal sorcery and Scion ritual magic.<br /> <br /> Either mortal sorcery is going to have to be its own thing, or, it is going to be something Scions don't bother with once they can grab Relics, or it's going to be grossly overpowered and relics get ignored.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To me, \u201chave different ritual requirements\u201d <i>is</i> \u201cdifferent rules\u201d. </div> </div> </div>But it is still window dressing and ultimately up to ST/player interpretation and definition. The books aren't going to waste the space to detail every last ritual for every Pantheon's multiple religions dedicated to them. At best, even in a fan-made system, you'd be looking at a list of culturally appropriate examples that people would hew as close to as they want.<br /> <br /> The thing is that, in the end, it isn't &quot;different rules.&quot; It is one rule: your Practices have to ritually match the style of magic you use. All the different ritual styles are window dressing on that rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It only detracts from my point if National Pantheons are still a thing in <b>Scion 2e</b>. </div> </div> </div>Or fictional Pantheons. Or the ability for Scions to grow up and start their own Pantheons instead of joining their parent's one.<br /> <br /> The whole point of all of those is simple: Scion isn't just about running ancient myths in modern times. It's about running your own versions of myths and playing with the myth structure by mixing in modern elements.<br /> <br /> There is absolutely nothing to gain by treating Scion as having to stick tightly to, &quot;a modern retelling of myth X, Y, and Z from different cultures happening at the same time.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have less of a problem with incorporating modern elements into traditional magical practices than I have with introducing whole new magical practices that are built around modern elements. </div> </div> </div>What's the difference? You seem to be trying to split hairs or create a dichotomy that I just don't see. Where is the line between a magical practice that is based in tradition but uses lots of modern elements, and a magical practice that uses modern elements to access traditional rituals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T10:24:28-08:00","id":9806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9763#post9763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having a way for mortal sorcerers to practice magic is a separate issue from using Practice to access Boons instead of Relics.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, they\u2019re fundamentally linked; see below. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9763#post9763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not arguing against mortal sorcerers; however I don't think your idea works as a combination of mortal sorcery and Scion ritual magic.<br /> <br /> Either mortal sorcery is going to have to be its own thing, or, it is going to be something Scions don't bother with once they can grab Relics, or it's going to be grossly overpowered and relics get ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly hope those aren\u2019t the only options, considering that the developers have said that they intend to have sorcery rules that apply to all of the tiers, not just <b>Origins</b>. That\u2019s why I\u2019m not particularly interested in arguments about why it won\u2019t work, except when offered in the spirit of describing the obstacles that need to be overcome: less \u201cit can\u2019t be done!\u201d and more \u201chow could we make this actually <i>work</i>?\u201d And frankly, that\u2019s what\u2019s been frustrating me about this topic: <i>it\u2019s going to happen,</i> and yet all anyone seems to be interested in talking about is why it won\u2019t work. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9763#post9763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it is still window dressing and ultimately up to ST/player interpretation and definition. The books aren't going to waste the space to detail every last ritual for every Pantheon's multiple religions dedicated to them. At best, even in a fan-made system, you'd be looking at a list of culturally appropriate examples that people would hew as close to as they want.<br /> <br /> The thing is that, in the end, it isn't &quot;different rules.&quot; It is one rule: your Practices have to ritually match the style of magic you use. All the different ritual styles are window dressing on that rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here, I think we\u2019re talking past each other. I suspect that what I\u2019m thinking of is a lot more similar to what you\u2019re advocating than you\u2019re making it sound. Conversely, you seem to be assuming that I\u2019m advocating something that would make <b>Exalted</b>\u2019s Charm Trees look simple. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9763#post9763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or fictional Pantheons. Or the ability for Scions to grow up and start their own Pantheons instead of joining their parent's one.</div> </div> </div> </div>FWIW, I have no interest in seeing entirely fictional Pantheons in any official material outside of a Shards-like supplement. I <i>would</i> like rules for founding a new Pantheon; but I\u2019d want said rules to be the sort of thing that Gods work toward as the conclusion of a massive chronicle, not something that a circle of scions do on a whim: it should be more akin to founding a new nation than setting up a book club. And outside of a Shards book, I\u2019m not particularly interested in any write-ups of Pantheons that have been founded in, say, the last five hundred years or so. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9763#post9763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole point of all of those is simple: Scion isn't just about running ancient myths in modern times. It's about running your own versions of myths and playing with the myth structure by mixing in modern elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is (or ought to be) <i>primarily</i> about ancient myths in the modern world; running your own versions of myths is what homebrewing is for, and playing with the myth structure is what Shards are about. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9763#post9763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is absolutely nothing to gain by treating Scion as having to stick tightly to, &quot;a modern retelling of myth X, Y, and Z from different cultures happening at the same time.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure there is: efficient use of page-count. I\u2019m not opposed to <b>Scion</b> supporting the things you\u2019re talking about somewhere down the road, in supplements dedicated to \u201calternate takes on <b>Scion</b>\u201d; but the four core books, at the very least, should stick tightly to \u201cancient myths in the modern world\u201d. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9763#post9763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the difference? You seem to be trying to split hairs or create a dichotomy that I just don't see. Where is the line between a magical practice that is based in tradition but uses lots of modern elements, and a magical practice that uses modern elements to access traditional rituals?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have a voodoo practitioner who uses technology to facilitate his practices, or who uses his practices on modern technology, he\u2019s still a voodoo practitioner. If you have a sorcerer whose concept of magic is that reality is a computer simulation and that magical practices are \u201ccheat codes\u201d, you have a magical practice that could not have existed even a hundred years ago. The latter is something for homebrew and Shards supplements; the former belongs in the core books. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T11:54:38-08:00","id":9881,"title":"","content":"The thing I think of most when contemplating the idea of &quot;magic&quot; in Scion is Odin's hanging on Yggdrasil to learn various things (songs, runes, et cetera) that had power in and of themselves, and were not part of the inherent power Odin possessed as a God. This kind of thing, the idea of a Wisdom in the world deeper than even the Gods can sometimes understand is where I think the idea of &quot;magic&quot; should exist in Scion as opposed to activation of divine abilities on the part of a given deity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T13:40:55-08:00","id":9959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/4986-magic-in-2e?p=9806#post9806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And frankly, that\u2019s what\u2019s been frustrating me about this topic: <i>it\u2019s going to happen,</i> and yet all anyone seems to be interested in talking about is why it won\u2019t work.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a big difference between your idea not being something I see working and me not seeing any option working. As far as I'm concerned the most likely option from the Scion team is going to be a separate power system ala Thaumaturgy/Sorcery in Exalted, or similar things from the WOD. I think the separate power subsystem is frustrating for a few reasons, but it is the only practical way I can see to accomplish what the devs have said they want.<br /> <br /> The important thing from that perspective is how to make it interesting without falling into the Exalted mode of Sorcery just being Charms with a twist that let you invest in just one area of power and still have lots of general application.<br /> <br /> It also very possible that mortal sorcery is going to scale in 2e, but not in terms of being a direct player power. It could be that part of a Scion's growth in power is a growth in the potency of the kind of magic their followers can use. A Hero's followers can only use small tricks, while a Demigod's followers have some punch, and a God's followers can access truly miraculous abilities with their magics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And here, I think we\u2019re talking past each other. </div> </div> </div>To an extent. But if we're talking past each other, lets go back to the initial point. Is there anything wrong with the cultural elements of Practices being window dressing as long as having consistent style is necessary?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> FWIW, I have no interest in seeing entirely fictional Pantheons in any official material outside of a Shards-like supplement.<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> It is (or ought to be) <i>primarily</i> about ancient myths in the modern world; running your own versions of myths is what homebrewing is for, and playing with the myth structure is what Shards are about.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Sure there is: efficient use of page-count. I\u2019m not opposed to <b>Scion</b> supporting the things you\u2019re talking about somewhere down the road, in supplements dedicated to \u201calternate takes on <b>Scion</b>\u201d; but the four core books, at the very least, should stick tightly to \u201cancient myths in the modern world\u201d. </div> </div> </div>I think this discussion would be less frustrating if you stopped trying to have your opinions on the game as things that the game &quot;ought&quot; to be to be held as the default. I get that you want these things out of the game, but I think you're making a fairly spurious argument that including a more flexible and malleable side of the game in the core rules detracts from the experience for those that don't want to use those elements. As Scion stands now, you can run a by-the-scrolls ancient myth based game just fine or a game that plays fast and loose with ancient and modern mythology. I don't see how that flexibility did anything to damage Scion as a whole or your ability to play it the way you want to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I <i>would</i> like rules for founding a new Pantheon; but I\u2019d want said rules to be the sort of thing that Gods work toward as the conclusion of a massive chronicle, not something that a circle of scions do on a whim: it should be more akin to founding a new nation than setting up a book club. And outside of a Shards book, I\u2019m not particularly interested in any write-ups of Pantheons that have been founded in, say, the last five hundred years or so. </div> </div> </div>I'm not advocating that starting your own Pantheon should be easy or simple. Just that if it is possible in the core rules, then the core rules should support options for this new modern age Pantheon; not have the support for it shoved off on a far off Shards like book. If I get to the point in a Scion game where my players have created a new Pantheon that has a much more digital age bend to it, I want to be able to play that out; including the rituals of their new followers, cults, and religions.<br /> <br /> Also, if we're looking at 500 years or so, you'd be comfortable with, say, a Humanist Pantheon organized around the Greeco-Roman Muses as representations of the worthy capabilities of humans rather than distinct deities to worship?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you have a voodoo practitioner who uses technology to facilitate his practices, or who uses his practices on modern technology, he\u2019s still a voodoo practitioner. If you have a sorcerer whose concept of magic is that reality is a computer simulation and that magical practices are \u201ccheat codes\u201d, you have a magical practice that could not have existed even a hundred years ago. The latter is something for homebrew and Shards supplements; the former belongs in the core books. </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the &quot;reality hacker&quot; concept is really just a modern day take on an ancient philosophic/mystic concept. The difference between Plato's Cave and reality being a computer simulation is the metaphor being used; not the philosophic underpinning of the mystic practice. This is another place to no dismiss Mage. The Technocracy, including the Sons of Ether and Virtual Adepts, trace their philosophy back to the ancient Greeks. They are following what they see as the logical extension of the evolution of ancient wisdom through the lenses of history and modern knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}